Two new files, deliberately tiny:

## File 1 (new): `Controller/PaymentController.java`

```java
package com.example.Used.Controller;

import com.example.Used.Model.Responses.PaymentResult;
import com.example.Used.Model.Responses.PaymentStatus;
import com.example.Used.Service.PaymentService;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

/**
 * POST /api/payments/{listingId}  -> 202 Accepted, hands off to the pool
 * GET  /api/payments/{id}         -> poll the outcome
 */
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/payments")
public class PaymentController {

    private final PaymentService paymentService;

    public PaymentController(PaymentService paymentService) {
        this.paymentService = paymentService;
    }

    @PostMapping("/{listingId}")
    public ResponseEntity<PaymentResult> buy(@PathVariable Long listingId) {
        PaymentResult result = paymentService.submitPayment(listingId);
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.ACCEPTED).body(result);
    }

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public PaymentStatus status(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return PaymentStatus.from(paymentService.getPayment(id));
    }
}
```

## File 2 (new): `Model/Responses/PaymentStatus.java` — polling DTO

```java
package com.example.Used.Model.Responses;

import com.example.Used.Model.Payment;

import java.time.LocalDateTime;

/** Polling answer: "is my payment done yet?" */
public class PaymentStatus {

    public Long paymentId;
    public Long listingId;
    public Payment.Status status;
    public String failureReason;
    public String amount;
    public LocalDateTime processedAt;

    public static PaymentStatus from(Payment p) {
        PaymentStatus s = new PaymentStatus();
        s.paymentId = p.getId();
        s.listingId = p.getListing().getId();
        s.status = p.getStatus();
        s.failureReason = p.getFailureReason();
        s.amount = p.getAmount().toPlainString();
        s.processedAt = p.getProcessedAt();
        return s;
    }
}
```

**Why a DTO instead of returning the `Payment` entity:** the entity's `listing`, `buyer` and `seller` are lazy-loaded relationships — returning it directly would either crash on serialization or leak the whole user table into your JSON. `PaymentStatus` shows exactly the 6 fields a buyer needs and nothing more.

**Why `POST /api/payments/{listingId}` and not a JSON body:** simplest possible contract — no request DTO, no validation layer. Your `Buy Now` button just needs one id in the URL.

