## How it works

```
Buyer submits COD
      │
      ├─ Email  ──────────────────────────────► seller's inbox
      ├─ SSE "COD_REQUEST" ───────────────────► floating card, bottom-right, on ANY page
      │                                          [thumbnail] "Ali wants 'City Bike FX2'"
      │                                          $250.00   [ Accept ] [ Decline ]
      └─ Profile → "COD requests" card ───────► full list, same two buttons
```

Clicking **Accept** calls `POST /api/payments/{id}/cod/accept`; the card turns green ("Accepted — the buyer has been notified") and the buyer's payment page flips to success on its next poll. **Decline** behaves the same way with a red state and a `COD_DECLINED` reason for the buyer. If the request was already handled (e.g. the seller clicked in two tabs), the card shows *"This request has already been handled."*

